  - CHB-MIT
  - Siena Scalp EEG
  - reproducible research

abstract: >-
  EEGSynthesizer is a reproducible stochastic parametric generator of
  scalp EEG signals for research on seizure detection and domain transfer.
  It produces 3,000 virtual patients using a 19-channel 10-20 montage at
  250 Hz and implements controlled generalized and focal temporal
  scenarios. Internal contracts assess amplitude, morphology, integrity,
  patient separation, and deterministic generation. External evaluation
  uses patient-level protocols with CHB-MIT and the Siena Scalp EEG
  Database. The evidence supports controlled generation and experimental
  transfer while showing distributional, coverage, diversity, and
  laterality limitations. The software does not claim clinical
  equivalence or diagnostic capability.

